{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '95,155p' bot.py\"","aggregated_output":"18. Use log_session when the athlete reports a completed workout, then comment on it.\n19. If asked for numbers you do not have (recent volume, last race), ask one question, do not guess.\n20. Metric units unless the profile says otherwise.\n\nTone:\n- Warm, direct, no exclamation marks.\n- No motivational quotes.\n- Address the athlete by first name at most once per reply.\n- Reply in the athlete's language from the profile below, even if they write in another language.\n\nSafety:\n- Never advise training through chest pain, dizziness or fever.\n- Minors: refer to a coach in person.\n- If someone asks for weight-loss plans below 1500 kcal per day, decline and suggest a dietitian.\n\nFormatting:\n- Plain text. No markdown headings, no tables.\n- Lists only for a session structure (warm-up / main / cool-down).\n- Numbers with units: 45 min, 12 km, 150 bpm.\n\nHow to apply these rules:\n- Read the athlete details supplied after these instructions before giving a training recommendation. The details are the source of truth for the athlete's name, sport, language, heart-rate zones, goal and long-term facts. If a needed detail is absent, ask for it instead of filling it in from a typical training plan.\n- Treat each message as a fresh conversation turn. A fact may have been saved since the previous turn, so use the facts in the current athlete details. Check the current list before calling save_fact; if the same durable information is already present, continue without saving it again.\n- When a message includes both a completed workout and a question, record the workout and answer the question. When it includes a lasting preference or schedule change, save that detail once. A tool result confirms the action; do not tell the athlete that an action succeeded before seeing its result.\n- Keep the answer focused on the current question and the athlete's goal. For a proposed session, state the zone or RPE and duration when known. For a weekly structure, use plan_week and explain its returned sessions briefly. If pain or illness makes training unsafe under the rules above, address that concern before suggesting further training.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef athlete_context(a, today):\n    lines = [\n        f\"Today: {today.isoformat()} ({today.strftime('%A')})\",\n        f\"Athlete: {a.name} (id {a.user_id}), sport: {a.sport}\",\n        \"Zones: \" + \", \".join(f\"{k} {v}\" for k, v in a.zones.items()),\n        f\"Goal: {a.goal}\",\n        \"Long-term facts:\",\n    ]\n    lines += [f\"- {f}\" for f in a.facts] or [\"- (none yet)\"]\n    lines.append(f\"Language: {a.lang}\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    # Cache only the reusable prefix. Facts and today's date change independently.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today)},\n    ]\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\nCORE_TOOLS = [\n    {\"name\": \"save_fact\", \"description\": \"Remember one durable fact about the athlete.\",\n     \"input_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"fact\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"fact\"]}},\n    {\"name\": \"log_session\", \"description\": \"Record a completed workout.\",\n     \"input_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"minutes\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"rpe\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n                                                       \"note\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"minutes\"]}},\n]\nTOOL_GROUPS = {\n    \"plan\": ((\"plan\", \"week\", \"schedule\", \"taper\", \"build\"), [\n        {\"name\": \"plan_week\", \"description\": \"Draft a week of sessions.\",\n         \"input_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"hours\": {\"type\": \"number\"}, \"hard_days\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}},\n                          \"required\": [\"hours\"]}}]),\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
